description:
**File:** rust/lichen-rpl/src/dodag.rs
**Lines:** 420-430

**Issue:** Collects addresses into a Vec, then iterates to remove. HashMap::retain would be more efficient.

```rust
fn prune_inadmissible_parents(&mut self) {
    let to_remove: Vec<[u8; 16]> = self
        .parents
        .iter()
        .filter(|(_, candidate)| !self.admissible(candidate))
        .map(|(addr, _)| *addr)
        .collect();
    for addr in to_remove {
        self.parents.remove(&addr);
    }
}
```

**Edge case:** On no_std embedded targets (which this crate supports via feature flags), unnecessary allocations matter.

**Fix:**
```rust
fn prune_inadmissible_parents(&mut self) {
    self.parents.retain(|_, candidate| self.admissible(candidate));
}
```

Note: This requires careful review of borrow patterns - `admissible` takes `&self` so retain's `&mut self` should work, but verify the admissible check doesn't need to reference parents.
